\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Noah's ark kept tossing,
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0 Stayed long on the seas;
\par Though it kept on tossing,
\par He was frightened not.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par If I should meet troubles
\par In the vale of death;
\par My consolation is;
\par God sees me each day.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The red sea did split up,
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0 Moses walked its depths.
\par The Israelites he led
\par trod the barren lands.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I, the forest dweller
\par Doth expect Jesus,
\par The Lord Christ my life is;
\par God takes care of me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jonah lay in the whales'
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0 Frightening dark belly;
\par But the Lord redeemed him,
\par Which was wonderful.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par If in my perturbance
\par I should be afraid,
\par The Lord Christ my life is,
\par Surely follows me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4. In the den of  Lions
\par \pard\li270\sl180\slmult0 Daniel found himself
\par The angel of the Lord
\par to his guide assur'd
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I shall enter death's vale
\par Thro' the Lord Jesus;
\par Even then, I know that
\par God shall be with me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  The colleagues of Daniel,
\par \pard\li270\sl180\slmult0 Gave praises to God.
\par From the fiery furnace,
\par They had salvation.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Should I pass through fire,
\par Remind me of them,
\par In my song to declare
\par That God is with me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Jesus' manger birth,
\par \pard\li270\sl180\slmult0 and his Gethsemane,
\par His death on the cross and
\par Burial in the tomb
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Clearly tell the story
\par Of our redemption.
\par It involves all mankind;
\par God is with us all.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Peter was put-in-chains,\cf0 
\par \pard\li270\sl180\slmult0 His bangles fell off
\par Paul was stoned yet got up
\par And unscathed he went;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Similarly, my foes
\par Cannot take my life;
\par Pleased I am to declare;
\par That God is with me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  8.  A hymn I'll sing to God
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0 And I'll give Him praise;
\par The devil gets angry,
\par My downfall he craves;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And he always tempts me;
\par My failure to cause.
\par In all these I shall say
\par \pard     That God is with me.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

